# CX1 scaling data — every number traces to a logged line cited below.
# Chart script scaling-cx1.py reads THIS file, fits k itself, and asserts
# against the LOGGED_K lines. No k value is hardcoded in the script.
#
# SOURCES
# BEFORE (bridge, k ~3.8):
#   docs/results/A6-FABRIC-EXPERIMENT.md, section "Arms B/C and DEV tuning --
#   BLOCKED (measured)": token-prefix truncation table from the
#   src/hearsay/examples/bridge_scale.rs probe (release, 1 core, lattice
#   data/lattices/dev5/1272-128104-0001.lat.jsonl, 9510 tokens / 7396 arcs,
#   ZERO arcs kept, real 72 MB LM). Same numbers in bead
#   hearsay-four-nlvs--fabric-performance-indexes NOTES "SCALE DATA from W4-real".
#   The 9510-token full-lattice point is a TIMEOUT (>900 s), excluded from the fit.
# AFTER (saturation rebuild, k ~1.07):
#   bead hearsay-four-nlvs--fabric-performance-indexes, comment 2026-11-03 20:43
#   "CX1 PER-PATH FINAL": RELEASE overall k=1.0727 (points 1k=0.086s, 10k=0.99s,
#   100k=12.0s; per-path ingest 1.0887 / attach 1.0751 / commit 1.0623 gated,
#   query+enforce VOID-immaterial); DEBUG overall k=1.0625 (points 0.66s / 8.25s /
#   88.1s). Paper docs/writeup/WRITEUP.md (abstract + section 9) reports 1.07.
#   Cloud cross-check (nlvs NOTES): k=1.11 release, 100k in 8.5 s (other machine).
#
# FORMAT: "<SERIES> <tokens> <wall_s>" data lines; "LOGGED_K <series> <k>"
# carries the bead-logged k for verification (tolerance 0.01 unless a
# LOGGED_TOL line widens it); "PAPER_K <k>" carries the paper's reported
# value (must equal round(logged_release, 2)).
# Series: BEFORE | AFTER_RELEASE | AFTER_DEBUG.
# BEFORE's LOGGED_K 3.8 is the prose claim ("k approx 3.8" in the nlvs bead
# DESCRIPTION, "about 3.8" in the paper abstract): no single fitted k was
# ever logged for the bridge, so the tolerance is 0.05 (1 decimal).
# CEIL lines are the CX1 gates (nlvs bead GATES + decision_cx1.rs ceiling).

